Hello World!

## Firecrawl example

A minimal example of using [Firecrawl](https://docs.firecrawl.dev) to scrape a
web page into clean, LLM-ready Markdown lives in
[`examples/firecrawl_scrape.py`](examples/firecrawl_scrape.py).

### Run it

    pip install -r requirements.txt
    cp .env.example .env        # then add your FIRECRAWL_API_KEY
    export FIRECRAWL_API_KEY="fc-..."   # get a key at https://firecrawl.dev

    python examples/firecrawl_scrape.py https://example.com

The script fetches the given URL (default: https://example.com) with Firecrawl's
`scrape` endpoint and prints the resulting Markdown. See the
[Firecrawl docs](https://docs.firecrawl.dev) for other endpoints (crawl, map,
search, extract).
